# Rental Account Management — Final Design (Draft, Not Activated)

Status: design only. No schema, migration, API, or UI activation. `prisma/schema.prisma` is unchanged.

## 1. Audit retention: `RentalAccountAuditLog` FK

Design decision: `ON DELETE RESTRICT` on `RentalAccountAuditLog.rentalAccountId → RentalAccount`.

Rationale: Hard-deleting an account would erase its audit trail. This contradicts the requirement that history is never lost.

Implementation:
- `RentalAccountAuditLog.rentalAccountId` is `NOT NULL` with `ON DELETE RESTRICT`, matching `rental_account_management.sql` and `RENTAL_SCHEMA_PROPOSAL.md`. Audit rows can never be orphaned; the referenced account must exist for every audit entry.
- Account retirement is performed via `isActive = false`, not hard delete. Because accounts are never hard-deleted in normal business workflows, the `RESTRICT` constraint never blocks routine operations while still protecting history.
- `accountCodeSnapshot` and `gameIdSnapshot` on audit rows preserve historical context if the account's code or game assignment is later modified.
- `rentalAllocationId` is intentionally NOT a foreign-keyed column on `RentalAccountAuditLog`. Adding such an FK would create a cycle with `RentalAllocation`/`Session` and risk orphaning audit rows when allocations are released. Instead, allocation/session correlation is captured in the human-readable `details` field (e.g. `Session cl... duration 60min`). `Session` and `RentalAccount` are both protected by `ON DELETE RESTRICT`.

This matches the SQL draft and proposal exactly and ensures audit rows cannot be orphaned.

## 2. Models

### RentalAccount
- `id String @id @default(cuid())`
- `gameId String` → `Game` (`ON DELETE RESTRICT`), back-relation `Game.rentalAccounts RentalAccount[]`
- `accountCode String @unique` (global unique, matches PC `stationNumber` convention, e.g. `CS2-01`)
- `status RentalAccountStatus @default(AVAILABLE)` (AVAILABLE, IN_USE, MAINTENANCE, OFFLINE — same semantics as PC/Console)
- `hourlyRate Float` (server-managed tariff, validated > 0)
- `secretRef String?` (URI reference only; never returned by API or logged)
- `notes String?` (internal notes; never contains credentials)
- `isActive Boolean @default(true)` (soft-delete flag; false means retired but data preserved)
- `createdAt`, `updatedAt`
- Indexes: `@@index([gameId])`, `@@index([status])`, `@@index([isActive])`, composite `@@index([gameId, status])`

### RentalAllocation
- `id String @id @default(cuid())`
- `rentalAccountId String` → `RentalAccount` (`ON DELETE RESTRICT`), back-relation `RentalAccount.rentalAllocations RentalAllocation[]`
- `sessionId String` → `Session` (`ON DELETE RESTRICT`), back-relation `Session.rentalAllocations RentalAllocation[]`
- `status RentalAllocationStatus @default(ACTIVE)` (ACTIVE, COMPLETED, CANCELLED)
- `allocatedAt DateTime @default(now())`
- `releasedAt DateTime?`
- `durationMinutes Int`
- `hourlyRateSnapshot Float` (rate copied at allocation time; source of truth stays `RentalAccount.hourlyRate` at that moment)
- Partial unique index: `UNIQUE ("rentalAccountId") WHERE "status" = 'ACTIVE'` (raw SQL, not expressible in Prisma schema; already in draft SQL)
- Price: NOT stored. Checkout total lives in `Session.totalPrice` → `Transaction.totalAmount`. Rental stores only the rate snapshot and duration; the amount is calculated at checkout as `round((Session.durationMinutes * Session.hourlyRate) / 60)`. Extension increments `Session.durationMinutes`, `Session.remainingMinutes`, and `Session.endTime` only; `Session.totalPrice` is NOT updated during extension and is recalculated at checkout. This integrates cleanly with the existing POS flow.

### RentalAccountAuditLog
- `id String @id @default(cuid())`
- `rentalAccountId String` → `RentalAccount` (`ON DELETE RESTRICT`), `NOT NULL`; audit rows can never be orphaned
- `accountCodeSnapshot String` (snapshot at time of action)
- `gameIdSnapshot String` (snapshot at time of action)
- `action String` (must match `RENTAL_ACCOUNT_AUDIT_ACTIONS`: CREATED, UPDATED, ALLOCATED, EXTENDED, RELEASED, CANCELLED, STATUS_CHANGED, DEACTIVATED)
- `previousStatus String?` (status before action)
- `newStatus String?` (status after action)
- `performedByUserId String` → `User` (`ON DELETE RESTRICT`), back-relation `User.rentalAuditLogs`
- `details String?` (human-readable context; never contains credentials)
- `createdAt DateTime @default(now())`
- Indexes: `@@index([rentalAccountId, createdAt])`, `@@index([createdAt])`

## 3. Pricing rule
- Rate comes only from `RentalAccount.hourlyRate` on the server. Client never sends rate (already removed from `allocateRentalSchema`).
- Snapshot `hourlyRateSnapshot` and `durationMinutes` at allocation.
- Extension: increment `Session.durationMinutes` and `Session.endTime`, but DO NOT update `Session.totalPrice`. The final price is calculated at checkout from the accumulated duration: `sessionPrice = round((durationMinutes * hourlyRate) / 60)`.
- Amount is settled through the existing `checkoutSession` POS/Transaction flow. Extension does not create a separate transaction or invoice.

## 4. Secret manager (fail-closed)
- `SecretManagerProvider` interface exists in `src/lib/secret-manager.ts`. Default is `UnconfiguredSecretManagerProvider`, which returns `null`.
- BLOCKER: no real provider is configured or integrated in this repository. Credential retrieval stays disabled.
- `secretRef` is stored as a reference only. It is stripped by `sanitizeRentalAccountForClient` and never logged.
- Credential retrieval restricted to ADMIN (recommended), with an audit row per access (no secret in details).

## 5. API plan (not implemented)
Base: `/api/rental-accounts`
- `GET` list (filters: gameId, status, q; pagination required)
- `POST` create (ADMIN/OPERATOR)
- `PATCH /[id]` update (rate, notes, status, isActive)
- `POST /[id]/allocate` body: sessionId, durationMinutes (no rate)
- `POST /[id]/extend`, `POST /[id]/release`, `POST /[id]/cancel`
- `GET /[id]/history`
- Status mapping via `apiErrorResponse`: validation 400, not found 404, double allocation / invalid state 409, unauthenticated 401, forbidden 403, internal 500 without details. Prisma P2002 maps to 409.

