## 7. Integration test design (to write with activation)
- Authorization: 401 without session, 403 for STAFF/unknown role.
- Concurrency: two parallel allocate calls for one account, exactly one succeeds, other 409.
- Pricing: rate from DB, client-supplied rate ignored.
- Extend, cancel, release: state transitions; release only when linked Session/Transaction is completed.
- Audit retention: deactivate account, history still readable; hard delete blocked by RESTRICT.
- All tests use mocks or a disposable database, never production.

## 8. Integration with existing POS checkout
- `extendRentalAllocation` accepts `rentalAccountId`, `sessionId`, `extraMinutes`, and `performedByUserId`; `extraMinutes` is an integer from 15 through 1440. It updates `Session.durationMinutes`, `Session.remainingMinutes`, and `Session.endTime` in one transaction. It does NOT update `Session.totalPrice` or create a separate `Transaction`.
- `checkoutSession` (in `src/services/session.service.ts`) recalculates final price from persisted `durationMinutes` and trusted `hourlyRate`, so extension is included once at checkout.
- `addSessionTime` currently updates `Session.totalPrice` directly. Before rental activation, add a server-side guard after loading the session: when an active rental allocation exists for the session, reject `addSessionTime` and require `extendRentalAllocation`. Do not rely on UI restrictions. Guard lookup and duration update must be covered by an integration test.
- The guard must preserve current non-rental `addSessionTime` behavior. Rental extension must use the rental transaction path, with audit write in the same transaction. Payment happens once at checkout.

